  "title": "Lightning strike at outstation, no licensed engineer on site",
  "narrative": "Faro, early afternoon, thunderstorms over the Algarve. AX-FAL, an A320, is struck by lightning on approach and parks on stand 4. The return ACX561 to Manchester is due at 13:50 with 176 passengers. Accent Air has no licensed engineer in Faro: the nearest B1 is in Lisbon (a long drive), another in Manchester could position on the afternoon flight ACX565. There is no spare aircraft in Faro. The operating crew reported at 09:00 in Manchester, so a long wait will run into their duty limit, and Manchester has a night curfew. The duty manager wants clear options: fly an engineer in, drive one down, or cancel and recover tomorrow.",
